* 3D mode 102 with overlap 2: no back-off; the result depends on whether the bucket query returns the die bottom faces below the workpiece nodes (hit -2 -> die 1 moved by (0,0,2)) or not (backward retry); discriminates flag 0 from flag 1
* ORACLE: die 1 moved by (0,0,2) back to contact (net z 4.4e-16): the bucket query returns the die bottom face behind the top workpiece nodes (same cell, OBJPOS_interference_kernels.md 2.4 / ik_m102_bucket2_3d), hit -2.
KFREAD 0
UPSET_Brick.KEY
OBJPOS 1 1 0 0 -2
OBJPOS 1 102 0.0 0 0 -1 2 0 0 0
KFWRIT
OUT.KEY
